soong_namespace {
}

// Derp: charger-token-boot handoff.
//
// A charger-token boot - cable inserted while the phone is powered off, so the
// bootloader comes up with androidboot.mode=charger - never starts Android on
// its own: init queues the "charger" event instead of "late-init", healthd
// takes the display, and zygote/system_server never start, so the phone sits
// on the charging animation until a long press.
//
// derp_charger_token.rc performs that handoff directly with two init builtins
// (class_stop charger, then trigger late-init) on ro.bootmode=charger. It is
// installed by device.mk via PRODUCT_COPY_FILES: an init rc needs neither an
// exec bit nor a binary, so no sh_binary module is involved.
//
// The earlier one-shot reboot guard is gone. It existed because both
// co-processors stayed dead after this handoff, but that failure is now fixed
// at the root in the kernel (s2mpu08_pmic_probe() used to clear the CP rails
// on every charger-token boot), and the guard also needed an exec type this
// user build does not have - it exec'd u:r:su:s0, while root here is
// u:r:ksu:s0, so it was a silent no-op anyway.
